title: Save the buffer.
pid: 114c0c64-ce3c-4327-9e9d-3e592d9d497f
body: |2-
  This causes the server to act on the merge request
  and rebuild the buffer.

  The nodeMerge is built after the save's other edits, so it keeps them.
  If the same save retitles the acquirer, or edits the acquiree's body,
  the merged node carries the new title,
  and the text preserver ("MERGED: ...") carries the edited body.
  If the same save deletes a node the acquirer or the acquiree contains,
  the merged node does not contain it.

  A save that deletes the acquirer or the acquiree itself is refused,
  and nothing is written: remove either the deletion or the merge
  request, then save again.
